104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (How these sources connect to this study: Belady's work gives the FIFO anomaly and the OPT benchmark. Denning's working set model gives the framework for the locality patterns I generate. The textbook explains why real systems approximate LRU rather than implement it exactly.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Textbook examples usually trace one short reference string, often fewer than 25 references. Such examples show a policy's behaviour on one input but say little about the average case. This study measures fault rates over 10,000 references, for five locality patterns, across five random seeds, and at five memory sizes. It asks how the ranking of the three policies changes as the locality pattern changes.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
