586 0 obj
<<
/Title (Uniform random\(H3\). FIFO and LRU differ by less than 0.1 percentage points at every frame)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 584 0 R
/Next 590 0 R
>>
endobj
587 0 obj
<<
/Title (Phased locality, 100% \(H4\). At 4 frames, below the working set of 8, every policy thrashes. FIFO and LRU fault on about 50% of references and OPT on 29%. At 8 frames, the three policies fall to about 1.5%, and they differ by at most 0.1 points. The remaining faults are first touches at the start of each phase. With 20 phases of 8 pages, the upper bound is 160 first touches, and the runs produce 145 to 157 faults. Clean locality makes the policy choice nearly irrelevant once memory fits the working set.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 584 0 R
/Prev 591 0 R
>>
endobj
588 0 obj
<<
/Title (Conclusion)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 584 0 R
/Next 592 0 R
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
<<
/Title (if pattern == "Sequential loop \(50 pages\)":)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 593 0 R
/Next 585 0 R
>>
endobj
590 0 obj
<<
/Title (count, so H3 holds. Recency gives LRU no advantage when every page is equally likely to return. OPT stays 15 to 33 points below both, which shows how much future knowledge is worth on this pattern.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 584 0 R
/Prev 586 0 R
/Next 594 0 R
>>
endobj
591 0 obj
<<
/Title (Phased locality, 90% \(H1, H2, H4\). At 8 frames, FIFO faults 32.0% of the time, LRU 24.9% and OPT 13.1%. Moving to 16 frames cuts LRU to 9.7% and FIFO to 15.3%. The gap narrows to 0.2 points at 64 frames, when memory is large enough to hold nearly all recent pages. The sharpest drop comes as the frame count rises past the working set size of 8. This supports H4.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 584 0 R
/Prev 595 0 R
/Next 587 0 R
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Title (Limitations and Future Work)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 588 0 R
/Next 596 0 R
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Title (return [rnd.randrange\(pages\) for _ in range\(length\)])
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 597 0 R
/Next 589 0 R
>>
endobj
594 0 obj
<<
/Title (Sequential loop. FIFO and LRU fault on every reference until memory holds all 50 pages, because each policy evicts the page the loop needs next. OPT keeps part of the loop in memory. At 32 frames it faults on 37% of references, against 100% for the other two. This pattern shows that LRU's recency rule can fail badly on a cyclic scan.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 584 0 R
/Prev 590 0 R
/Next 595 0 R
>>
endobj
595 0 obj
<<
/Title (Skewed workload \(H1, H2\). LRU beats FIFO at every frame count. At 16 frames, FIFO faults on 34.8% of references and LRU on 24.1%, a gap of 10.7 points. LRU sits 9.4 points above OPT at that size, while FIFO sits 20.1 points above. H1 and H2 hold on this pattern.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 584 0 R
/Prev 594 0 R
/Next 591 0 R
>>
endobj
